      {
        "thread_id": "TH1",
        "thread_goal": "Align on current issues and approve target workflow scope",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M1",
            "speaker_id": 20729,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi team, let's kick off the standardisation project. To start, what are the biggest pain points you face with the current front-of-house workflow? Thinking about everything from prescription drop-off to finding OTC items. This will help us scope out the new SOPs for A1.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "wave",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 84286,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Definitely the time it takes to find things that have been moved. And when shelf fillers put new stock in the wrong place. Also, the handover process for prescriptions is messy.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 55101,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "From my side, the issue is not having a standard place for everything. Sometimes I have to move items to make space for a delivery because the shelves are disorganised. A clear map would solve this.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "point_up",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 12454,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "I agree with the point about finding things. Sometimes customers are waiting and I can't find a common item. Is T1 where we are supposed to be listing these things?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 20729,
            "reply_to": "M4",
            "text": "Exactly, @12454. All this feedback is the input for T1. Keep it coming.",
            "mentions": [
              12454
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M6",
            "speaker_id": 255566,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "The lack of a clear procedure for when a medicine is out of stock. Different people say different things to customers.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M7",
            "speaker_id": 84286,
            "reply_to": "M6",
            "text": "Yes! And checking expiry dates is very ad-hoc.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M8",
            "speaker_id": 32339,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Sorry for the delay. Another issue is inconsistent labelling on the shelves themselves. Sometimes the label is for an old product.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M9",
            "speaker_id": 20729,
            "reply_to": "M8",
            "text": "Great points, everyone. I'm hearing a few key themes:\n1. Inconsistent stock location & difficulty finding items.\n2. Unclear processes for stock-outs and handovers.\n3. Inaccurate shelf labelling and expiry checks.\n\nI propose we prioritise these three as our main focus for the new workflow. Any objections?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D2"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M10",
            "speaker_id": 55101,
            "reply_to": "M9",
            "text": "That covers the main issues from a stocking perspective. Works for me.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M11",
            "speaker_id": 12454,
            "reply_to": "M9",
            "text": "Sounds good.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thumbsup",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M12",
            "speaker_id": 84286,
            "reply_to": "M9",
            "text": "Yes, let's do it.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M13",
            "speaker_id": 20729,
            "reply_to": "M9",
            "text": "Excellent. So, to formalise it, our scope for standardisation will cover: (1) Prescription intake and collection, (2) OTC query and sale, (3) Stock reception and shelving, and (4) Daily stock verification. This will be the core of the A1 document.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
